    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "therapists just tell me to 'cope' or 'find a new hobby'. they don't get it. it's not about being sad, it's about being finished. the person who was an athlete, the person who had a purpose... that person is dead. i'm just a shell inhabiting a ruined body, stuck in a loop of pretending to be alive. it feels so heavy, carrying around a life that doesn't even belong to me anymore. it feels like there's no point to the aftermath.",
